  "scope_id": "CLASSK-DICHOTOMY-20261026-001",
  "title": "A dichotomy for counting maps to class-(K) groups with bounded homology, on closed manifolds and knot groups",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold and knot groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "For coprime class-2-by-cyclic groups of class (K) over odd prime fields with r | p - 1, counting homomorphisms from closed 3-manifold groups with bounded first homology, and from knot groups, is #P-hard exactly when a commutator joins two nontrivial characters with nontrivial product (else polynomial), via sector partition functions isolated over disjoint unions and Bulatov-Grohe. Hence Rowell's 2009 conjecture fails for every such group unless every #P function is polynomial-time computable.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
